{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788378914251176001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"unmelted-grieving-blowfish","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":6,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"8aac504823ec2949231ceaf2ef1ed2a3f6ddfe3bab7fe1a6ab67e96c9c97265d","event_uuid":"38033a20-a39a-47db-bb14-17dc8a364777","position":{"commit_sha":"3eb404fab0953d77b5ddffa42388030203ea2df5","position":"1788375027122404696-38033a20-a39a-47db-bb14-17dc8a364777"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"14614c950a3a863c8aab8d4950fae22b995e297e386a3b0ab0394d2d094fe8d6","event_uuid":"948b0fab-c1cf-4555-bb83-34eab1a835c8","position":{"commit_sha":"0c31932d5ea274036d6cafea81b26acfb15931c1","position":"1788375086906199373-948b0fab-c1cf-4555-bb83-34eab1a835c8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"94f5e2a678eb8a5e77c3a98870a45ed13cb752a70e84b01e472f6edf23609f6b","event_uuid":"42c5f41d-cfef-4cdf-8ba0-5762c4df660c","position":{"commit_sha":"3f6263cd0e6382fc4007044c4a4a92dbf6cf74c8","position":"1788375230069290935-42c5f41d-cfef-4cdf-8ba0-5762c4df660c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"11cf4ca1d8ab0fd7208d9aab9993e9d0ff78e605e91dbd384ebb08351a34f126","event_uuid":"b2ce0b5d-44cd-4fa0-8499-b0e64fcaf4ad","position":{"commit_sha":"b4b2138e71d42b4194c7b678db4610c1e8d83b5b","position":"1788375841848215876-b2ce0b5d-44cd-4fa0-8499-b0e64fcaf4ad"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"c8c127a3015c40586dc64d036676f42f3f1c413661303b2d5a1b7d2873eb8927","event_uuid":"2743053a-88cf-45a6-a7e5-203210f889e9","position":{"commit_sha":"b5aceb3252bc194eb43d3c672c5a8c14a067768e","position":"1788375888512860203-2743053a-88cf-45a6-a7e5-203210f889e9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"ceb1733297086c1814a40961deb40c274feeace79903c5a8ee75f6a9b6466b97","event_uuid":"cdf36e91-dcdf-40e9-9aba-8398a078be1f","position":{"commit_sha":"8158f6738c927bfe61b53e5ef4d20c0241bc8632","position":"1788376362604815975-cdf36e91-dcdf-40e9-9aba-8398a078be1f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788375027122404696,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[],"description":"# S4 — Bound `/var/tmp` growth and alarm on tmp saturation\n\n## Why\n`/var/tmp` is a root-volume accumulator from the incident. Age-only cleanup is not enough if the generator can fill the disk before files age out, and aggregate root alarms do not identify tmp saturation.\n\n## What\nAdd `/var/tmp` age cleanup plus an actual size ceiling compatible with the host filesystem. Use systemd-tmpfiles for age cleanup, and implement the byte cap with a quota-capable mount/path or a bounded host cleanup service/timer if tmpfiles alone cannot enforce size on the deployed filesystem. Extend observability to publish `/var/tmp` usage/cap and add a dedicated CloudWatch alarm.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: tmpfiles/timer/quota configuration, observability metric, Terraform alarm, runbook policy, and tests. Out of scope: `/var/gerrit` data-volume probe policy (linked sibling `scowlful-bovine-dragonfly`), review scratch volume, Docker cache, journald, and writable container layers.\n\n## Grounding\n- Current observability reports only aggregate filesystems: `infra/scripts/observability.sh:72-90`.\n- systemd-tmpfiles docs support age-based cleanup entries and btrfs qgroup helpers, but qgroup helpers do not create an XFS byte cap by themselves.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `/var/tmp` has documented age cleanup and an actual enforced size ceiling on the Gerrit host.\n- [ ] The implementation states why the chosen size mechanism works on AL2023/root filesystem assumptions.\n- [ ] Observability publishes `/var/tmp` usage/cap metrics and Terraform adds a dedicated alarm wired to SNS.\n- [ ] Runbook documents safe remediation and forbids `/var/gerrit` as generic investigation scratch.\n- [ ] Targeted tests cover cleanup/quota/timer config, metric emission, and alarm wiring.\n- [ ] Portability criterion: uses Linux host-level facilities and local tests; no GitHub-only CI signal is introduced.\n\n## Design Ambiguity\nThe approved design names \"systemd-tmpfiles age+size\". Tmpfiles supplies age cleanup, but on root/XFS a separate byte-cap mechanism may be needed; the implementing story must choose and justify that mechanism.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/scripts/compose-up.sh","reason":"Install tmpfiles/timer/quota config or invoke common host disk-ceiling installer."},{"path":"infra/scripts/install-disk-ceilings.sh","reason":"Potential new host provisioning helper for /var/tmp cleanup/quota."},{"path":"infra/scripts/observability.sh","reason":"Publish /var/tmp usage/cap metric."},{"path":"infra/terraform/monitoring_autodeploy.tf","reason":"Add /var/tmp saturation CloudWatch alarm."},{"path":"infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md","reason":"Document /var/tmp cap/alarm and safe scratch policy."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_observability_disk_pressure.py","reason":"Cover /var/tmp metric emission."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_alarm_actions_terraform.py","reason":"Assert new alarm action wiring."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","6202-e1c7-c57f-4897"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"6202-e1c7-c57f-4897","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["infra","gerrit","disk-ceiling","tmpfiles"],"ticket_id":"2ba3-bf77-1303-4b2d","ticket_type":"story","title":"S4 — Bound /var/tmp growth and alarm on tmp saturation","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/scripts/test_observability_disk_pressure.py tests/unit/test_alarm_actions_terraform.py","dd_id":"AC4","dd_text":"/var/tmp metric and alarm are covered."},{"command":"terraform -chdir=infra/terraform validate","dd_id":"AC5","dd_text":"Terraform syntax remains valid."}]},"source_event_uuids":["38033a20-a39a-47db-bb14-17dc8a364777","948b0fab-c1cf-4555-bb83-34eab1a835c8","42c5f41d-cfef-4cdf-8ba0-5762c4df660c","b2ce0b5d-44cd-4fa0-8499-b0e64fcaf4ad","2743053a-88cf-45a6-a7e5-203210f889e9","cdf36e91-dcdf-40e9-9aba-8398a078be1f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788378914251176001,"uuid":"9a5a21ab-6ef7-4072-9559-ca195fecf26c"}